From: Jack Kingston <998656+jkingston@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] board: trimui-brick: boot product rootfs from SD

The stock firmware stores its root filesystem in ext4 rather than asking the
boot firmware to preload it into RAM.  Follow that hardware behaviour for the
larger product image: boot brick-diag from the fixed SD root partition and
retain the bounded initramfs path for brick-previous/brick-baseline recovery.

The WPE-enabled cpio is 298 MiB uncompressed and 95 MiB compressed.  Loading
it in U-Boot delayed Linux past the observed power-on window and also consumed
RAM needed by the browser.  The kernel already has built-in ext4 and MMC
support, so this changes packaging and boot policy without changing hardware
configuration.

Signed-off-by: Jack Kingston <998656+jkingston@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 configs/trimui-brick_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/configs/trimui-brick_defconfig b/configs/trimui-brick_defconfig
--- a/configs/trimui-brick_defconfig
+++ b/configs/trimui-brick_defconfig
@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@ CONFIG_CMD_BOOTCOUNT=y
 CONFIG_USE_BOOTCOMMAND=y
 CONFIG_HUSH_PARSER=y
 CONFIG_SUPPORT_RAW_INITRD=y
-CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="gpio set PH3; sleep 0.12; gpio clear PH3; setenv kernel_addr_r 0x42000000; setenv fdt_addr_r 0x44000000; setenv ramdisk_addr_r 0x50000000; for brick_bootdir in brick-diag brick-previous brick-baseline; do for brick_initramfs in initramfs.cpio.zst initramfs.cpio.gz; do if load mmc 0:1 ${kernel_addr_r} ${brick_bootdir}/Image && load mmc 0:1 ${ramdisk_addr_r} ${brick_bootdir}/${brick_initramfs} && setenv diag_rdsize ${filesize} && load mmc 0:1 ${fdt_addr_r} ${brick_bootdir}/brick-usb.dtb && fdt addr ${fdt_addr_r} && fdt resize 4096 && fdt rsvmem add 0x48000000 0x40000; then setenv bootargs console=ttyS0,115200 quiet loglevel=3 vt.global_cursor_default=0 rdinit=/init brick.bootdir=${brick_bootdir}; booti ${kernel_addr_r} ${ramdisk_addr_r}:${diag_rdsize} ${fdt_addr_r}; fi; done; done; echo SD boot failed; while true; do sleep 1; done"
+CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="gpio set PH3; sleep 0.12; gpio clear PH3; setenv kernel_addr_r 0x42000000; setenv fdt_addr_r 0x44000000; setenv ramdisk_addr_r 0x50000000; for brick_bootdir in brick-diag brick-previous brick-baseline; do if test ${brick_bootdir} = brick-diag; then if load mmc 0:1 ${kernel_addr_r} ${brick_bootdir}/Image && load mmc 0:1 ${fdt_addr_r} ${brick_bootdir}/brick-usb.dtb && fdt addr ${fdt_addr_r} && fdt resize 4096 && fdt rsvmem add 0x48000000 0x40000; then setenv bootargs console=ttyS0,115200 quiet loglevel=3 vt.global_cursor_default=0 root=/dev/mmcblk0p2 rootfstype=ext4 rootwait rw brick.bootdir=${brick_bootdir}; booti ${kernel_addr_r} - ${fdt_addr_r}; fi; else for brick_initramfs in initramfs.cpio.zst initramfs.cpio.gz; do if load mmc 0:1 ${kernel_addr_r} ${brick_bootdir}/Image && load mmc 0:1 ${ramdisk_addr_r} ${brick_bootdir}/${brick_initramfs} && setenv diag_rdsize ${filesize} && load mmc 0:1 ${fdt_addr_r} ${brick_bootdir}/brick-usb.dtb && fdt addr ${fdt_addr_r} && fdt resize 4096 && fdt rsvmem add 0x48000000 0x40000; then setenv bootargs console=ttyS0,115200 quiet loglevel=3 vt.global_cursor_default=0 rdinit=/init brick.bootdir=${brick_bootdir}; booti ${kernel_addr_r} ${ramdisk_addr_r}:${diag_rdsize} ${fdt_addr_r}; fi; done; fi; done; echo SD boot failed; while true; do sleep 1; done"
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_LIMIT=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_FS=y
 CONFIG_BOOTCOUNT_BOOTLIMIT=1
-- 
